---
source: crates/mwf/tests/cli.rs
expression: self.transcript
---
$ mwf --help
mwf: a project-local wiki engine for coding agents

Usage: mwf [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init       Create .mwf/ in this git repository root
  show       Print a page: frontmatter, body, rev, links out and links in
  search     BM25 search over pages; the words of QUERY are joined with spaces
  list       List pages by slug
  index      Print the table of contents rendered from the current pages
  log        Print the last N lines of log.md, oldest first
  lint       Check every page; exits 1 when there is an error
  new        Create a page; the body is read from stdin
  write      Replace a page's body with stdin, if REV is still its rev
  patch      Replace the one occurrence of OLD in a page's body with NEW
  set        Change frontmatter fields
  archive    Set a page's status to archived
  unarchive  Set a page's status back to active
  rename     Rename a page and rewrite the links to it
  delete     Move a page to .mwf/trash/
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json     Print `{"ok": true, "data": …}` or `{"ok": false, "error": …}` instead of text
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Host integration (dispatched before the commands above):
  install    Add mwf's hooks and skill to a host: mwf install --host claude|codex [--dry-run]
  uninstall  Remove them: mwf uninstall --host claude|codex [--dry-run]
  hook       Run by the host's hooks, not by hand: mwf hook <event> --host claude|codex
`mwf install --help` and `mwf uninstall --help` describe both.
[exit 0]

$ mwf new --help
Create a page; the body is read from stdin

Usage: mwf new [OPTIONS] --type <TYPE> --title <TITLE> --summary <SUMMARY> <SLUG>

Arguments:
  <SLUG>  The new page's slug: a-z, 0-9 and -

Options:
      --json               Print `{"ok": true, "data": …}` or `{"ok": false, "error": …}` instead of
                           text
      --type <TYPE>        preference, decision, knowledge, incident or task
      --title <TITLE>      The page title
      --summary <SUMMARY>  One line saying what the page is about; shown in index.md and search
                           results
      --tag <TAG>          A tag; repeat for more
  -h, --help               Print help
[exit 0]

$ mwf patch --help
Replace the one occurrence of OLD in a page's body with NEW

Usage: mwf patch [OPTIONS] <SLUG>

Arguments:
  <SLUG>  The page's slug

Options:
      --json             Print `{"ok": true, "data": …}` or `{"ok": false, "error": …}` instead of
                         text
      --old <OLD>        The text to replace; it must occur exactly once in the body
      --old-file <PATH>  Read OLD from a file
      --new <NEW>        The replacement text
      --new-file <PATH>  Read NEW from a file
  -h, --help             Print help
[exit 0]

$ mwf search --help
BM25 search over pages; the words of QUERY are joined with spaces

Usage: mwf search [OPTIONS] <QUERY>...

Arguments:
  <QUERY>...  Words to search for

Options:
      --json             Print `{"ok": true, "data": …}` or `{"ok": false, "error": …}` instead of
                         text
      --type <TYPE>      Only pages of this type; repeat to allow several
      --tag <TAG>        Only pages with this tag; repeat to require several
      --status <STATUS>  Which pages by status [default: active] [possible values: active, archived,
                         all]
      --limit <N>        Maximum number of results [default: 10]
  -h, --help             Print help
[exit 0]
